## CWE rule
CWE-89 — SQL Injection
Description: A SQL query is built from untrusted input without parameterization, allowing the structure of the query to be altered.
Vulnerability indicators:
- Concatenation, % formatting, str.format or f-strings with external data inside the SQL string
- Parameters coming from request/argv/form reach execute() without parameter binding
- snprintf/sprintf used to compose the query before mysql_query/sqlite3_exec
Safe patterns:
- Parameterized queries or prepared statements with placeholders (%s, ?, :name) and values passed separately
- ORM with parameterized filters

